      "text": "10. Performance, Feed Scale, and Real-Time",
      "fontSize": 30,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "10. Performance, Feed Scale, and Real-Time",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "5992be4ab559462c8caf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1014.3341070884949,
      "y": 2547.34639545231,
      "width": 870,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aa",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2,
      "version": 75,
      "versionNonce": 155858877,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784064218973,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Feed-scale decisions\n• Avoid one global subscription per poll\n• Subscribe only while visible / recently visible\n• Pause updates for offscreen polls\n• Preserve option ordering during live updates\n• Use stable keys\n• Memoize only after measuring\n• Virtualize only when feed size justifies complexity\n• Avoid expensive animations on every count change\n\nReal-time transport\n• Polling: simplest, higher staleness / overhead\n• SSE: ideal for server → client result updates\n• WebSocket: useful if app already has bidirectional infra\n\nPerformance metrics\n• Poll render duration\n• Interaction to Next Paint\n• Selection → submit latency\n• Mutation failure rate\n• Duplicate submission rate\n• Optimistic rollback rate\n• Subscription count per viewport",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Feed-scale decisions\n• Avoid one global subscription per poll\n• Subscribe only while visible / recently visible\n• Pause updates for offscreen polls\n• Preserve option ordering during live updates\n• Use stable keys\n• Memoize only after measuring\n• Virtualize only when feed size justifies complexity\n• Avoid expensive animations on every count change\n\nReal-time transport\n• Polling: simplest, higher staleness / overhead\n• SSE: ideal for server → client result updates\n• WebSocket: useful if app already has bidirectional infra\n\nPerformance metrics\n• Poll render duration\n• Interaction to Next Paint\n• Selection → submit latency\n• Mutation failure rate\n• Duplicate submission rate\n• Optimistic rollback rate\n• Subscription count per viewport",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
