      "index": "ao",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1293851987,
      "version": 296,
      "versionNonce": 786441107,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784064705178,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** Real-time updates ****\n* Periodic polling\n* Server-Sent Events\n* WebSocket subscriptions\n\n- SSE is sufficient when updates flow primarily from the server to the client. \n- WebSockets become more useful when the product already maintains bidirectional real-time infrastructure.\n- Updates should not aggressively move result bars while a user is trying to vote. Before voting, the UI may preserve option ordering and update only counts.\n\n===============================================================\n\n*** Feed-scale rendering ***\n* Avoid creating one global subscription per poll\n* Subscribe only to visible or recently visible polls\n* Pause updates for offscreen polls\n* Use stable option keys\n* Memoize result rows only after measuring\n* Avoid expensive animations for every update\n* Virtualize only when the feed size and item complexity justify it\n-- Consistency\nVote counts are inherently concurrent. The client should not attempt to maintain globally exact totals.\n-- The server should:\n* Enforce one vote per user when required\n* Apply idempotency keys\n* Atomically record the vote\n* Return canonical updated results\n* Resolve expiration and permission checks\n=====================================================================\n\n*** Performance metrics *** \n* Poll render duration\n* Time from selection to submission\n* Vote API latency\n* Vote failure rate\n* Duplicate-submission rate\n* Optimistic rollback rate\n* Poll interaction INP\n* Percentage of users who select but do not submit\n\n*** Security ***\nThe client cannot enforce vote integrity. The backend must validate:\n* Poll existence\n* Option membership\n* User authorization\n* Poll expiration\n* Duplicate voting rules\n* Rate limits\n* Idempotency tokens\n* All labels and poll questions should be rendered as text rather than injected HTML unless sanitized.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** Real-time updates ****\n* Periodic polling\n* Server-Sent Events\n* WebSocket subscriptions\n\n- SSE is sufficient when updates flow primarily from the server to the client. \n- WebSockets become more useful when the product already maintains bidirectional real-time infrastructure.\n- Updates should not aggressively move result bars while a user is trying to vote. Before voting, the UI may preserve option ordering and update only counts.\n\n===============================================================\n\n*** Feed-scale rendering ***\n* Avoid creating one global subscription per poll\n* Subscribe only to visible or recently visible polls\n* Pause updates for offscreen polls\n* Use stable option keys\n* Memoize result rows only after measuring\n* Avoid expensive animations for every update\n* Virtualize only when the feed size and item complexity justify it\n-- Consistency\nVote counts are inherently concurrent. The client should not attempt to maintain globally exact totals.\n-- The server should:\n* Enforce one vote per user when required\n* Apply idempotency keys\n* Atomically record the vote\n* Return canonical updated results\n* Resolve expiration and permission checks\n=====================================================================\n\n*** Performance metrics *** \n* Poll render duration\n* Time from selection to submission\n* Vote API latency\n* Vote failure rate\n* Duplicate-submission rate\n* Optimistic rollback rate\n* Poll interaction INP\n* Percentage of users who select but do not submit\n\n*** Security ***\nThe client cannot enforce vote integrity. The backend must validate:\n* Poll existence\n* Option membership\n* User authorization\n* Poll expiration\n* Duplicate voting rules\n* Rate limits\n* Idempotency tokens\n* All labels and poll questions should be rendered as text rather than injected HTML unless sanitized.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
